;; The registry of built-in types and functions (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.3): each file of the runtime
;; declares its types as package variables made by NewBuiltinType (no slots: slots are set in the file's
;; init function, after every type exists, so the slots' functions may name any type) and registers
;; its built-in functions with RegisterBuiltin. The builtins module of an Interp is made from the
;; registry: every registered type and function whose name is public, in registration order.

